WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.049
Zack Snyder’s Justice League’s convoluted
production process and the fan campaigns for

00:00:05.049 --> 00:00:10.660
its release have made it a particularly interesting
specimen in the already pretty fascinating

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:16.500
superhero movie genre, and to make the most
of a unique situation, Snyder seemingly used

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.490
every opportunity to cram the four-hour film
full of neat stuff.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.840
There are numerous changes from the theatrical
version and cool Easter eggs – and even

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:30.160
a brand new epilogue scene that teases a grim,
apocalyptic future in which a potty-mouthed

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:35.000
Batman and a long-haired, weary Joker team
up to battle an evil Superman.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.090
Among the many new characters the Snyder Cut
brings into the fold is Darkseid, the interplanetary

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.810
warlord behind the movie's main villain, Steppenwolf.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.660
Darkseid drops by near the end of the movie,
rocking up to the action with his two major

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.120
lieutenants flanking him.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:55.220
The creepy, robed guy on the tyrant's right-hand
side is Desaad, Darkseid's sadistic assistant.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.000
But who's the white-haired old lady rounding
up the trio?

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.830
And as a fair warning, try not to laugh at
her name.

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:05.400
The lady in question is Granny Goodness, a
perennial contender for the worst misnomer

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.560
in the entire DC universe.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:12.101
She may look like a sweet old lady, and her
name may suggest that's entirely true, but

00:01:12.101 --> 00:01:13.540
she's anything but.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:18.260
This granny won't bake you cookies and slip
a $20 bill into your bag after you visit her

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.630
"just in case you need pocket money" — oh
no, she'll mess your whole life up while keeping

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:24.430
a smile on her face.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:29.690
Created by comic book legend Jack Kirby, who's
credited both as the writer and artist behind

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:35.390
the character, Granny Goodness made her DC
Comics debut in 1971's Mister Miracle Vol.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:36.570
1 #2.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:40.970
She's a New God originating from the planet
Apokolips, and started off as a member of

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.310
the "Lowlies" class.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:46.880
When she was plucked from the peasants around
her to become a "Hound" for Darkseid, Granny

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.860
Goodness' life and fate changed.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:54.330
She established herself as an incredibly ruthless,
manipulative, and dangerous woman as she became

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:58.940
the trainer and commander of Darkseid's elite
forces — a job that she accomplishes by

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:04.420
brainwashing innocent orphans into obedient
killing machines in his "orphanage" facilities.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:09.149
What's worse, her torturous training methods
and unrepentant, sadistic nature are directly

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:12.049
contradicted by her gentle, sweet manner.

00:02:12.049 --> 00:02:15.659
Granny Goodness even takes her appearance
from that of the late comedian and actress

00:02:15.659 --> 00:02:20.019
Phyllis Diller, who wouldn't hurt a fly unless
she could make it laugh beforehand.

00:02:20.019 --> 00:02:24.540
Basically, imagine Dolores Umbridge from the
Harry Potter film franchise, add superpowers

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.329
and elite military training in place of magic,
and equip her with several torture dungeons

00:02:29.329 --> 00:02:32.290
and battalions of elite troops she has at
her disposal.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.879
That's Granny Goodness.

00:02:33.879 --> 00:02:37.939
What little we see of Granny in Zack Snyder's
Justice League makes her seem like a more

00:02:37.939 --> 00:02:41.459
physically imposing figure than her comic
book counterpart.

00:02:41.459 --> 00:02:45.510
And while the Snyder Cut of Justice League
does mark Granny Goodness' live-action film

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.349
debut, it's not the first time she's appeared
in the flesh on viewers' screens.

00:02:49.349 --> 00:02:55.629
That happened just once prior, in the penultimate
season of the CW superhero series Smallville,

00:02:55.629 --> 00:03:00.480
starring Tom Welling as Clark Kent in his
years living in Kansas before he becomes Superman.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.639
Two different actresses portrayed Smallville's
Granny, and the depiction of the character

00:03:04.639 --> 00:03:09.279
leaned pretty heavily on the sinister end
of the sweet-old-lady-ruthless-manipulator

00:03:09.279 --> 00:03:10.279
dichotomy.

00:03:10.279 --> 00:03:15.909
In Smallville, Nancy Amelia Bell brought Granny
Goodness to life in the season 9 finale, "Salvation,"

00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:20.310
in which her face isn't seen but the markers
of her outwardly sweet side — knitting needles

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:22.889
and a cozy, covered-up outfit — were.

00:03:22.889 --> 00:03:27.359
Christine Willes took over the role thereafter,
making her the literal face of Smallville's

00:03:27.359 --> 00:03:32.559
Granny — the prim and proper Head Administrator
of St. Louise's Orphanage who's secretly a

00:03:32.559 --> 00:03:38.150
cunning master manipulator with powerful telepathic
and telekinetic abilities, along with a number

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.400
of other powers.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:44.260
A season 10 episode reveals that one of the
children at St. Louise's Orphanage was Tess

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:49.089
Mercer, who – spoiler alert — is really
Lutessa Luthor, the daughter Lionel Luthor

00:03:49.089 --> 00:03:52.449
had with Pamela Jenkins, his son Lex's nanny.

00:03:52.449 --> 00:03:56.510
Tess lived at the orphanage from the time
she was five years old to when her biological

00:03:56.510 --> 00:04:00.370
father returned and took Tess out of Granny
Goodness' care.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:04.529
Before Tess left, Granny erased nearly all
of her memories so that she wouldn't remember

00:04:04.529 --> 00:04:06.709
her life before the Mercers adopted her.

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:10.900
We’re not sure if there will be a sequel
to Synder’s Justice League, but if anyone

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.900
wants to make use of the character in future
projects, Granny Goodness would certainly

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:19.440
make for a menacing, scheming villain that
would scare just about anyone who crosses

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.440
her path.

